      "title": "THUDM/IndexCache",
      "url": "",
      "publishedDate": "2026-03-13T00:00:00.000Z",
      "summary": "The IndexCache project by THUDM introduces a method to significantly accelerate sparse attention mechanisms, specifically DeepSeek Sparse Attention (DSA), used in large language models like DeepSeek-V3.2 and GLM-5. It achieves this by reusing token index computations across layers, exploiting the high overlap (70–100%) in selected tokens between adjacent layers. This approach reduces redundant indexer calculations by up to 75%, leading to up to 1.82× faster prefill and 1.48× faster decoding speeds with minimal impact on output quality. The method involves partitioning layers into full layers that compute indices and shared layers that reuse cached indices, with options for training-free or training-aware implementations. The technique is validated on models up to 744B parameters, offering substantial speedups in long-context inference scenarios, and can be integrated into existing SGLang and vLLM frameworks with a straightforward patch.",
